plays.verse:
We stand upon earth and dream's the stage;
Our palms like knives that pierce the night—खंजर’s kiss,
And sleep we call the breathless sigh of winds.

drafts.tidy:
We stand upon earth and dream's the stage;
Our palms like knives that pierce the night—खंजर’s kiss,
And sleep we call the breathless sigh of winds.

We are such stuff as dreams are made,
Upon the stage of fate's swift kiss;
And when the clash begins now—

plays.verse:
Not Caesar's name I mourn with tears so deep,
But Rome’s sweet heart beats faster than my sighs;
In blood we wrought the world today, in fire we bled—

