drafts.raw:
Come, you spirits that tend on mortal thoughts, unsex me here;
Unwear my shame, I will show my might;
Let us clash our swords as kings once fought in bold denial;
With fire and fate we'll make this fate anew.

ताज, सिंहासन की चमक में,
लालसा की धारा में मंडराती,
डायन ने देखा था, राजा की घबराय हुई,
नए ख़्वज पर मिट्टी

drafts.tidy:
Come, you spirits that tend on mortal thoughts, unsex me here;
Unwear my shame, I will show my might;
Let us clash our swords as kings once fought in bold denial;
With fire and fate we'll make this fate anew.

Spoken here in verse where pride may blouse,
Thou must heed this threat ere fear will grow;
I warn thee now as storms do howl and roar:

Many tears have washed this morning's dew,
Sir, thou standest bold, but soft thy soul will show;
Yet I shall not yield to sorrow's plea.
